guamp: client Metal devices get a writable cache directory and Turnip shader cache (port of codex/gpu-upstream2-20261029 0008)

fin43: Maps and Photos open slowly; the render server has its m2v directory and MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR (V row cache hit116
miss0), clients had neither, so every launch compiled every pipeline from NIR to IR3 again. Applies after 0001-0003, 0009-0013.

diff --git a/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm b/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
index e03de5b..a38a1f6 100644
--- a/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
+++ b/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
@@ -208,6 +208,22 @@ static id clientDevice(unsigned port) {
         strlcat(candidates[i], "m2v", sizeof candidates[i]);
         mkdir(candidates[i], 0700);
         if (access(candidates[i], W_OK) != 0) continue;
+        // guamp (UniXNU-guamp patches/adreno-metal/0008): access() passes where the sandbox still refuses the write (AegirPoster, widgets),
+        // so a file is really made here first; and Turnip's on-disk shader cache goes into the same directory, as in the render server.
+        // A client had none: MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR unset, Mesa's default ($HOME/.cache) is outside what a sandboxed extension may write, so
+        // every launch compiled its pipelines again on the main thread (AegirPoster killed by PosterBoard's 5 s snapshot timeout inside
+        // libvulkan_freedreno). An explicit MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR in the environment wins.
+        {
+            char probe[600];
+            snprintf(probe, sizeof probe, "%s/.probe-XXXXXX", candidates[i]);
+            const int fd = mkstemp(probe);
+            if (fd < 0) continue;
+            close(fd);
+            unlink(probe);
+        }
+        setenv("MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR", candidates[i], 0);
+        // Bounded per process (Mesa's default is 1 GiB): the directory is the process's own (container) cache, kept across boots.
+        setenv("MESA_SHADER_CACHE_MAX_SIZE", "64M", 0);
         ++usable;
         @try {
             device = native_bridge_metal_open(turnip, candidates[i], registryID, nullptr);
